From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:41:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Nintendo DS platform

Makefile.nds builds a DSi enhanced .nds with devkitARM and libnds/calico,
on top of a few engine changes:

- The zone takes all free RAM, 4 MiB on the DS and 16 MiB on the DSi,
  I_Quit returns to the homebrew launcher, I_Error shows the message on
  the touch screen and the startup banner fits the 32 column console.
- FixedDiv uses the hardware divider, the ARM9 has no divide instruction.
- The 32-bit DG_ScreenBuffer and SDL_mixer are left out, and .gitignore
  no longer hides the doomgeneric/ source directory.

The platform itself:

- Video: the 320x200 frame is scaled to the top screen by the affine
  background hardware, smoothed by a half pixel offset second layer that
  is alpha blended on top (nds_smooth), with Doom's palette in the
  hardware palette.
- Touch screen: live automap or level stats panel drawn with the WAD's
  own font, a touch bar for weapons, map and zoom, and dragging the stylus
  turns the player.
- Sound: effects on hardware channels 0-7. MUS and MIDI music drive a
  wavetable synth on channels 8-15 from a 140 Hz thread.
- Speed: the column, span, wall and BSP renderer runs from ITCM.
- Startup: indexes every IWAD and mod (PWAD) in NitroFS and on the SD card
  in a picker that shows each game's title picture, runs mods on a
  matching IWAD, shows a loading screen and keeps config and saves in
  /data/doom/.
